- ### Sources
+ ### Sorgenti

- The generator behind a scope is chosen by an import from the package `randomization`. The
- secure generators draw from the JDK's
- [cryptographically secure](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cryptographically_secure_pseudorandom_number_generator)
- source, for values which an adversary must not predict:
+ Il generatore dietro un ambito si sceglie con un import dal package `randomization`. I
+ generatori sicuri attingono alla sorgente
+ [crittograficamente sicura](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cryptographically_secure_pseudorandom_number_generator)
+ del JDK, per valori che un avversario non deve poter prevedere:

= source, for values which an adversary must not predict:
=
- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Import
+ column  Import

- column  Generator
- column  Reproducible
- row  `seededRandomization`  ordinary, from the `Seed` in scope  yes
- row  `unseededRandomization`  ordinary  no, it varies run to run
- row  `secureUnseededRandomization`  secure  no
- row  `stronglySecureRandomization`  the platform's strongest secure source  no
+ column  Generatore
+ column  Riproducibile
+ row  `seededRandomization`  ordinario, dal `Seed` nell'ambito  sì
+ row  `unseededRandomization`  ordinario  no, varia da un'esecuzione all'altra
+ row  `secureUnseededRandomization`  sicuro  no
+ row  `stronglySecureRandomization`  la sorgente sicura più forte della piattaforma  no

- row
+ row

-   cell  `secureSeededRandomization`
+   cell  `secureSeededRandomization`

